• `event_date`: filter by calendar month ( '202011' , '202012' , '202101' )  
• `event_name`: keep only the purchase events (`event_name = 'purchase'`)  
• `user_pseudo_id`: identify each customer and connect the products bought in the same purchase (or in the same session if desired)  
• `items`: repeated RECORD that holds every product bought in one event  
    • `items.item_name`: product description – use to find “Google Red Speckled Tee” and to list the “other” products  
    • `items.quantity`: quantity of each product bought  
    • `items.item_id`, `items.item_category*`, `items.price`, … (can help to verify uniqueness / do extra analyses)  

Typical conditions you will need  
• `event_name = 'purchase'`  
• `LOWER(i.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'` (or `LIKE '%google red speckled tee%'`) to detect the tee  
• `event_date BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20210131'` or month substrings (`SUBSTR(event_date,1,6) IN ('202011','202012','202101')`)  
• To obtain “other products”, use the same purchase that contains the tee and exclude the tee itself: `LOWER(other.item_name) <> 'google red speckled tee'`  

